-- title:
--   Supersingular reduced field as a Drinfeld quotient field, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix the prime $q$ with $q=3$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, and with $j$-value in $\mathrm{ssJSet}$), assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and fix $s \in W$. Let $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be an intermediate field over $\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element of $A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; let $K_b$ be the bottom intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $k_0$, $A_b$ the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, assumed a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by a non-zero $\varpi_b$. Give $k_0$ the algebra structure on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ coming from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ and valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F_0 = \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, with $W_0 \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$, with $W_0$ a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; for every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion of $A_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $B$ contained in $W_0$ and $W_0$ equal to the set of ratios $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$, with $B$ stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for all $\zeta : \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and with the following chart datum: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, every witness that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$ is a domain and every $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,C_s$ with $\#C_s = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, kernel the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, with $\rho$ on $A_b$ given by reduction $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, with every element of the target a ratio of values of $\rho$, with the image of $\rho$ exactly the elements of the target lying in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$ in the Drinfeld function field, and with $\rho \circ \mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ equal to $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ of $(\gamma \bmod q, 1)$ applied to $\rho$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\gamma \bmod q, 1) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$; then for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with reduced field $F_{ss}$ such that $R.\mathrm{integers} \cap F_0 = W_0$, and for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, every domain witness for $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$ and every $\zeta$, there exist $C_s$ and a $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-algebra isomorphism $e : F_{ss} \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,C_s$ with $\#C_s = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ such that, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $(\gamma \bmod q, 1) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, the automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ induced on $F_{ss}$ by that level automorphism is carried by $e$ to the action of $(\gamma \bmod q, 1)$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   This identifies the residue (reduced) field of a regular prolongation of $A$ at a supersingular place of the full-level modular curve with a fixed-field quotient of the Drinfeld function field, together with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance of that identification, the data being read off an affine chart $B$ of the semistable model; it is the $q=3$ case, where the auxiliary level condition $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $\ell_g \mid M'$ is imposed. It feeds the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation rings and smooth-point stalks at the auxiliary level $k_0$.
